    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 004 and 006 (R-16), for #76 child E2. Evaluation runs each configuration N times from a declared repeat source (deterministic replay, captured historical run sets, or live runs once spec 026 is implemented), reports per metric and per slice the mean, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, a pooled estimate and a case-clustered percentile bootstrap interval computed with a named, versioned, seeded generator, and derives declared noise bands. Adds named baselines (`rustev.baseline/1`), a reproducibility check, diffs in JSON and Markdown, multi-candidate comparison, held-out accounting against a host-kept ledger file, and a declarative selection gate (`rustev.selection-gate/1`) with stated CI exit codes. Every existing document, gate and CLI output keeps its bytes. Answers spec 023's open question 3. Approved (A-25); approval authorizes no live run, provider call or spend, no quality claim, and no change to `rustev.eval-report/1` or any plan identity.\n",
    "title": "Evaluation repeatability, baselines, diffs and selection gates (amends 004 and 006)"
  },
